<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <!-- One key, and this file exists only to carry it.

         GENERATE_INFOPLIST_FILE is still YES for this target: every other key
         in the built bundle — CFBundleIdentifier, WKApplication,
         WKCompanionAppBundleIdentifier, the version pair, UIDeviceFamily — is
         synthesized from build settings, and Xcode MERGES those into this file
         rather than replacing it. That merge is the whole reason this can be
         two lines instead of the forty the phone's Info.plist carries.

         The key is here rather than as INFOPLIST_KEY_FarCoolerAppGroup because
         that setting DOES NOT WORK, and does not work quietly.
         `INFOPLIST_KEY_<key>` is not a general mechanism: Xcode honors it only
         for keys it already knows, and a custom key is dropped with no warning
         and no error. Verified against the built bundle — with the setting and
         no file, `plutil -p` on FarCoolerWatch.app/Info.plist showed
         WKCompanionAppBundleIdentifier present (a key Xcode knows) and
         FarCoolerAppGroup absent entirely.

         What that costs if it is ever "simplified" back to a build setting:
         `SnapshotStore.groupIdentifier` reads this key by name and returns nil
         when it is missing, so `SnapshotStore.read()` answers "nothing known"
         — the identical answer it gives when no snapshot has ever arrived. The
         watch draws its empty state forever on a phone that is sending
         perfectly well, and nothing in any log distinguishes the two cases.

         `$(FARCOOLER_APP_GROUP)` and not a literal: four channels, four groups,
         and this is the same expression the entitlement expands, so the
         container the code asks for and the container the signature grants
         cannot come to differ. -->
    <key>FarCoolerAppGroup</key>
    <string>$(FARCOOLER_APP_GROUP)</string>
</dict>
</plist>
